{"title":"Career roadmap · Print Production Manager","role":"Print Production Manager","summary":"A Print Production Manager plans, coordinates and controls printing operations from prepress through production, finishing and dispatch. The role combines printing technology, production planning, quality control, materials, machinery, costing, scheduling, people management and process improvement.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Printing & Packaging Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This is a directly aligned career, although Print Production Manager is usually a mid-career position. A graduate typically enters through roles such as Graduate Engineer Trainee, Production Executive, Production Engineer or Printing Technologist and progresses into management."},{"type":"h","text":"Typical production flow:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Customer Requirement","Prepress","Proofing","Plate/CTP","Printing","Finishing","Quality Inspection","Packing","Dispatch"]},{"type":"h","text":"Career-route check"},{"type":"note","label":"Starts","text":"Year 1"},{"type":"note","label":"Current degree","text":"B.Tech / B.E. Printing & Packaging Technology"},{"type":"note","label":"Desired career","text":"Print Production Manager"},{"type":"flow","items":["Printing & Packaging","Production","Operations Management"],"label":"Career cluster"},{"type":"note","label":"Entry accessibility","text":"Direct field; manager-level role is a longer-term destination"},{"type":"note","label":"Typical entry titles","text":"Graduate Engineer Trainee, Production Trainee, Production Executive, Printing Technologist, Production Engineer, Prepress Executive"},{"type":"note","label":"Assumption","text":"four-year B.Tech/B.E. beginning in 2026, graduating around 2030."}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career direction"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build printing, packaging, production, quality, machinery and process-management fundamentals."}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Work in print production and develop expertise in scheduling, press operations, quality, costing and shop-floor management."}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Progress toward Senior Production Engineer, Production Supervisor, Assistant Production Manager or Production Manager."}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Lead large printing operations, multi-line production, automation, digital printing, sustainability and operational excellence."}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"Printing fundamentals, engineering mathematics, chemistry and materials"},{"text":"NPTEL","url":"https://nptel.ac.in/"},{"text":"Printing-process notes/project"},{"text":"Technical foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 2"},{"text":"Paper, ink, substrates and basic printing processes"},{"text":"NPTEL + laboratory work"},{"text":"Substrate/ink comparison"},{"text":"Materials knowledge"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 1"},{"text":"Prepress, typography, colour science and image reproduction"},{"text":"NPTEL + practical lab"},{"text":"Prepress workflow project"},{"text":"Prepress capability"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 2"},{"text":"Offset, flexography, gravure and digital printing"},{"text":"Industry exposure + lab"},{"text":"Compare four printing processes"},{"text":"Press knowledge"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 1"},{"text":"Packaging production, finishing and converting"},{"text":"NPTEL + industry"},{"text":"Packaging production project"},{"text":"Production breadth"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 2"},{"text":"Production planning, scheduling, quality and costing"},{"text":"Industry + ASQ","url":"https://asq.org/"},{"text":"Production schedule + QC dashboard"},{"text":"Operations capabi